    <p>To understand why our platform excels at **<a href="/">cloud file sharing</a>**, it is important to compare architectures. In traditional **<a href="/">cloud file sharing</a>** (Google Drive, Dropbox, etc.), your file goes through a three-step relay: (1) your device uploads the file to a central server, (2) the file sits on the server waiting for the recipient, (3) the recipient downloads from the server. This relay architecture means your effective throughput is limited to the slowest step — usually your upload speed. It also means your data sits on a third-party server, raising privacy concerns. And it means you are paying for storage capacity even when you just need transfer capability. Our P2P **<a href="/">cloud file sharing</a>** approach compresses steps 1 and 3 into a single direct transfer: your device sends directly to the recipient's device through our encrypted relay. We don't need to permanently store your file. This means faster transfers, zero storage costs to recoup, no storage limits, and better privacy. This is the next evolution of **<a href="/">cloud file sharing</a>**, available right now at Send-Anywhere.in.</p>

